      "narration": "Anthropic asked the model to design protein binders — small proteins built to lock onto one target, which is how medicine often starts. Most designs simply don't stick, which is why ten or fifteen per hundred counts as normal. Across twelve targets, Fable 5.1 got close to fifty per hundred. That's three to five times the usual hit rate.",
