      "narration": "Those two lines separate because a cached re-read now costs twenty-five cents per million tokens instead of a dollar. So this is not a price cut — it's a discount on repetition. Look at the rest of the sheet: sending the model text is still ten dollars a million, getting text back is still fifty, and neither of those moved a cent. Only the re-reading got cheaper, which is why your bill drops on long sessions and barely moves on short ones.",
